+    <h2>1. An Overview of Data Protection &amp; Privacy by Design</h2>
+    <p><strong>General Information</strong></p>
+    <p>The DevTools Times is engineered around the core principles of <strong>Privacy by Design</strong>, <strong>Data Minimization</strong>, and <strong>User Transparency</strong>. We collect only the minimum data strictly necessary to provide requested features, disable optional third-party tracking and advertising scripts by default, and give you clear, granular control over your privacy preferences at all times.</p>
+
+    <h2>2. Data Minimization in Account Registration &amp; Sign-In</h2>
+    <p><strong>What We Collect and Why</strong></p>
+    <p>When you create an account or sign in via our Sign-Up and Sign-In forms, we collect only two fields:</p>
+    <ul>
+        <li><strong>Username:</strong> A user-selected identifier (we recommend using a pseudonymous handle rather than your real name or email address).</li>
+        <li><strong>Password:</strong> Used exclusively to authenticate your account.</li>
+    </ul>
+    <p>We do not require or collect your email address, phone number, physical address, or demographic profile. Authentication requests are sent with credentials omitted from cross-site contexts (<code>credentials: 'omit'</code>) and with referrer headers stripped (<code>referrerPolicy: 'no-referrer'</code>), and form interactions are marked with <code>data-skip-tracking="true"</code> so they are never captured by analytics scripts.</p>
+
+    <h2>3. Cookies, Local Storage &amp; Session State</h2>
+    <p><strong>Lazy Session Initialization (No Tracking Cookies by Default)</strong></p>
+    <p>Merely browsing articles on The DevTools Times does not set tracking cookies or initialize server-side session cookies. A strictly necessary session is created lazily only when you actively bookmark an article to save it to your personal Reading List.</p>
+    <p><strong>Privacy Consent Preferences</strong></p>
+    <p>Your choices regarding optional third-party scripts are stored locally in your browser under the <code>devtools_times_privacy_consent</code> key in <code>localStorage</code>. You can review or revoke these preferences at any time using the <strong>Manage Privacy Preferences</strong> button in the site footer.</p>
+
+    <h2>4. Third-Party Scripts, Analytics &amp; Advertising</h2>
+    <p><strong>Strictly Opt-In Third-Party Scripts</strong></p>
+    <ul>
+        <li><strong>Third-Party Advertising (<code>ad-client.js</code>):</strong> Disabled by default. Ad slots remain inactive unless you explicitly opt in to optional advertising via the Privacy Preferences panel.</li>
+        <li><strong>Third-Party Analytics (<code>analytics-client.js</code>):</strong> Disabled by default. The analytics script is only loaded if you explicitly grant consent AND your browser does not send a <strong>Do Not Track (DNT)</strong> or <strong>Global Privacy Control (GPC)</strong> signal. When loaded, it uses <code>crossorigin="anonymous"</code> and <code>referrerpolicy="no-referrer"</code>.</li>
+        <li><strong>Web Fonts:</strong> Fonts loaded from Google Fonts use anonymous cross-origin connections and a <code>no-referrer</code> policy to minimize metadata disclosure.</li>
+    </ul>
+
+    <h2>5. Document Security &amp; Privacy Headers</h2>
+    <p>Every response from The DevTools Times includes hardened HTTP headers to protect your privacy and security:</p>
+    <ul>
+        <li><code>Content-Security-Policy</code>: Restricts script, style, font, image, and network connections to trusted origins and blocks framing (<code>frame-ancestors 'none'</code>).</li>
+        <li><code>Permissions-Policy</code>: Explicitly disables sensitive browser APIs and tracking mechanisms, including <code>browsing-topics=()</code>, <code>geolocation=()</code>, <code>camera=()</code>, <code>microphone=()</code>, <code>identity-credentials-get=()</code>, and <code>storage-access=()</code>.</li>
+        <li><code>Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin</code>: Prevents full article URLs and paths from leaking to external origins.</li>
+        <li><code>X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff</code>, <code>X-Frame-Options: DENY</code>, <code>Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin</code>, <code>Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin</code>, and <code>Strict-Transport-Security</code>.</li>
+        <li><code>Cache-Control: no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate, private</code> on authentication pages (<code>/signin</code>, <code>/signup</code>) and user-specific endpoints (<code>/api/reading-list.json</code>).</li>
+    </ul>
+
+    <h2>6. Your Rights &amp; Controls</h2>
+    <p>You have the right to use The DevTools Times without optional tracking, to inspect and clear your local reading list and consent preferences at any time, and to use browser-level privacy signals (such as Global Privacy Control and Do Not Track), which we honor automatically.</p>
